  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Omega Canis Majoris",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Canis Major",
    "summary": "Omega Canis Majoris is a solitary, blue-white-hued star in the equatorial constellation of Canis Major. Its name is a Bayer designation that is Latinized from ω Canis Majoris, and abbreviated Omega CMa or ω CMa. This star is visible to the naked eye with an apparent visual magnitude of about 4. Based upon an annual parallax shift of 3.56 mas as seen from Earth, this system is located roughly 920 light-years (280 pc) away from the Sun. It is drifting further away with a line of sight velocity of 23 km/s.",
    "intro": "Omega Canis Majoris is a solitary, blue-white-hued star in the equatorial constellation of Canis Major. Its name is a Bayer designation that is Latinized from ω Canis Majoris, and abbreviated Omega CMa or ω CMa. This star is visible to the naked eye with an apparent visual magnitude of about 4. Based upon an annual parallax shift of 3.56 mas as seen from Earth, this system is located roughly 920 light-years (280 pc) away from the Sun. It is drifting further away with a line of sight velocity of 23 km/s.\n\n",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omega_Canis_Majoris",
